Teach the concept below as if to someone partway through a 6-week SQL + Next.js learning plan, building a Student Management System.

**Structure (keep each section short):**
1. **One-line definition.**
2. **Why it exists** — the problem it solves.
3. **Worked example** — using the project schema (students, courses, enrollments, grades). Show real SQL or real TSX, not pseudocode.
4. **Common gotcha** — the mistake beginners make with this.
5. **Practice exercise** — one prompt the user can run against their own DB. Do NOT give the answer.

Skip theory the user can't act on this weekend. Tie everything to PostgreSQL + Next.js App Router.

